`ifndef HI3516V100_CRG_RDL
`define HI3516V100_CRG_RDL

regfile eCRG {
    name = "Clock and reset generator (CRG), Hi3516 V100";
    desc = "
    PERI_CRG0..PERI_CRG43 clock/reset block at 0x20030000 (41 registers are implemented; PERI_CRG9, 40, 41 do not exist). The Hi3516 V100 is a single-chip Full-HD IP-camera SoC (one Cortex-A9, 800/750 MHz max). This file follows the ORIGINAL CHINESE data sheet (Hi3516 Full-HD IP-Cam SOC user guide, document version 00B60, 2011-08-12), chapter 3.2 (clock) and 3.2.5 (register description); names and descriptions are translated to English. Data sheet checked 2026-11-09. The register layout is NOT the Hi3520D one: the PLL blocks and the PERI_CRG numbering look alike but offsets and contents differ (here: 4 PLLs, A9 mode at PERI_CRG8, PLL lock bits at PERI_CRG43/0xAC, SFC at PERI_CRG25/0x64). The vendor U-Boot header `arch-hi3520d/platform.h` (4e4o-hi3520d-uboot tree; identical copies in arch-godarm, arch-godnet) carries exactly this Hi3516 layout (REG_CRG0/1/6/7 values, CRG8 A9 mode bits, CRG10 DDR ratio, CRG43 lock mask 0xF), which matches the reset values below. That header is an unused leftover inherited from a Hi3516-family template: no code in the tree references those macros, and the real Hi3520D vendor code uses the Hi3520D layout instead (U-Boot board/hi3520d/board.c uses PERI_CRG57; the vendor kernel mach-hi3520d/core.c reads the A9:AXI mode at CRG+0x28 bits 3:2 and its platform.h has no CRG macros besides the base). It is evidence about the Hi3516 template, not about the Hi3520D. No vendor Hi3516 V100 clock driver exists in the local OpenIPC trees.

    Clock sources: XIN (fixed 24 MHz crystal, the PLL reference), VIU0_CLK/VIU1_CLK (video input clocks), RGMII_RXCK/RGMII_TXCK (GMAC interface clocks). Four PLLs with two registers each: APLL = PERI_CRG0/1 (A9, DDR controller and bus clocks), VPLL0 = PERI_CRG2/3 (VOSD), VPLL1 = PERI_CRG4/5 (VOHD), EPLL = PERI_CRG6/7 (GMAC/PCIE). VCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv, which must be within 800 MHz..2.4 GHz.

    Reset frequencies (computed from the reset values): APLL VCO 800 MHz (refdiv 3, fbdiv 100, postdiv 1 x 1 -> POSTDIV 800 MHz); VPLL0 VCO 1080 MHz (POSTDIV 540 MHz); VPLL1 VCO 1188 MHz (POSTDIV 148.5 MHz); EPLL VCO 1500 MHz (POSTDIV 500 MHz, the fixed source of the SIO mclk dividers). Fixed module clock sources named by the data sheet: 24 MHz, 100 MHz, 148.5 MHz (NFC/SFC/CIPHER), 270 / 300 MHz (JPGE, MD, TDE, IVE), 396 / 360 / 300 MHz (VEDU), 74.25 / 148.5 MHz (VOU), 500 MHz (SIO mclk).

    CPU: the A9 runs from the 24 MHz crystal after reset (SLOW mode). Bring-up order: program PERI_CRG0/1 (only while in SLOW mode), wait 0.1 ms and check PERI_CRG43 bit 0, set PERI_CRG8 a9_max_freq_mode (before the SLOW -> NORMAL switch; 0 = 800 MHz with APLL POSTDIV 800 MHz, 1 = 750 MHz with POSTDIV 1500 MHz) and a9_axi_freq_mode (A9:AXI 1:1 .. 4:1), then switch the system controller to NORMAL (SC_CTRL mode). DDR: PERI_CRG10 ddrc_freq_mode (DDR PHY:AXI = 2:1 or 1:1). Bus/APB: the data sheet gives no APB divider and no UART clock select in the CRG; UART0..3 (PERI_CRG33..36), I2C (PERI_CRG37), SSP0/1 (PERI_CRG28/29), DMA (PERI_CRG27), PWM/EFUSE (PERI_CRG26) and IR/RTC/CIPHER (PERI_CRG38) have only a clock gate and a soft reset bit each. Flash: NAND controller PERI_CRG24 (24 MHz or 100 MHz), SPI NOR controller PERI_CRG25 (2X clock 24 / 100 / 148.5 MHz). Ethernet: PERI_CRG21 (gmac_txclk_mode MII / RGMII 10/100/1000, clock gate, reset). SDIO0/1: PERI_CRG32 (24/25 MHz or 50 MHz, polarity, gate, reset). USB 2.0 host: PERI_CRG30, everything is in reset after power-up; un-reset order: wait >= 10 us, usbphy_port0/1_treq, usbphy_req, wait 250 us, usb_ctrl_utmi0/1_req and usb_ctrl_hub_req, usb_ahb_srst_req (data sheet 10.7.3).

    Conventions: every *_srst_req bit is 1 = reset, 0 = deassert reset (the reset is not released automatically) and every *_cken bit is 1 = clock on, except where marked otherwise (vedu_srst_req and jpge_srst_req in PERI_CRG18/19 and vi_dll_rst in PERI_CRG16 have the inverted polarity as printed in the data sheet; low confidence).

    Known data sheet inconsistencies are listed in the register descriptions: PERI_CRG8 cpu__srst_req resets to 1; PERI_CRG16 vi_dll_rst text vs reset value; PERI_CRG13/14 bit 16/15 duplicated descriptions; PERI_CRG32 24 vs 25 MHz and SDIO1 reset copy error; PERI_CRG39 sense_cksel lists 27 MHz twice; PERI_CRG43 offset wraps in the summary table; PLL formula and VPLL1 example typos (3.2.3).
    ";

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG0 is the APLL configuration register 0.

APLL (PERI_CRG0/1) feeds the A9, the DDR controller and the bus clocks. Reset: postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 1, refdiv = 3, fbdiv = 100 -> VCO 24 x 100 / 3 = 800 MHz, POSTDIV output 800 MHz, which is the A9 clock in `max 800 MHz` mode (PERI_CRG8 a9_max_freq_mode = 0). For 750 MHz mode (a9_max_freq_mode = 1) FOUTPOSTDIV must be 1500 MHz (data sheet 3.2.3). Reset 0x89000000 is the REG_CRG0_VALUE constant in the vendor U-Boot header arch-hi3520d/platform.h (an unused Hi3516-template leftover, see the block description). PLL arithmetic (data sheet 3.2.3, Tables 3-2 and 3-3): the reference clock is XIN, a fixed 24 MHz crystal; FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv and must be >= 800 MHz and <= 2.4 GHz; FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2) (the data sheet prints `FOUTVCO / pstdiv1 * pstdiv2`, a typo for the product); FOUT1PH0 = FOUTVCO / (pd1 x pd2 x 2); FOUT2 = /(pd1 x pd2 x 4); FOUT3 = /(pd1 x pd2 x 6); FOUT4 = /(pd1 x pd2 x 8). The *_pd, *_foutvcopd, *_postdivpd and *_fout4phasepd bits are output enables (1 = running, 0 = powered down). A PLL configuration may only be changed in SLOW mode (the A9 then runs from the 24 MHz crystal); wait 0.1 ms and check the lock bit in PERI_CRG43 before switching back to NORMAL.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG0 (offset 0x0, printed page 3-16, `hi3516v100--Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 10200).";

        field {
            name = "Reserved in the bit table";
            desc = "Reserved in the bit table, but the data sheet total reset value of this register has these bits set (reset 0x1).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_nz_31_31[31:31];

        enum PERI_CRG0_apll_bypass_enum {
            no_bypass = 0x0 { name = "Not bypassed"; desc = "not bypassed"; };
            bypass = 0x1 { name = "Bypassed"; desc = "bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "APLL clock divider bypass control";
            desc = "APLL clock divider bypass control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG0_apll_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_bypass[30:30];

        field {
            name = "Second-stage output divider";
            desc = "Second-stage output divider (POSTDIV2) of the APLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_postdiv2[29:27];

        field {
            name = "First-stage output divider";
            desc = "First-stage output divider (POSTDIV1) of the APLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "Fractional part of the APLL multiplication factor";
            desc = "Fractional part of the APLL multiplication factor (frac / 2^24)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG0 @ 0x0000;

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG1 is the APLL configuration register 1.

Reset 0x006C3064 equals REG_CRG1_VALUE in the vendor U-Boot header arch-hi3520d/platform.h (unused Hi3516-template leftover). Reset gives refdiv 3, fbdiv 100 (VCO 800 MHz, see PERI_CRG0). Bit 22 reads 1 at reset although the bit table calls it reserved. [inferred] The Hi3520D/Hi3518 PLL registers have dsmpd at this bit (1 = integer mode, reset 1) and dacpd at bit 23; this data sheet documents neither, so treat bit 22 as probably dsmpd and leave it at 1. To stop the APLL write bit 21 = 0 (data sheet 3.10.4).

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG1 (offset 0x4, printed page 3-17, `hi3516v100--Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 10246).";

        field {
            name = "Reserved in the bit table";
            desc = "Reserved in the bit table, but the data sheet total reset value of this register has these bits set (reset 0x1).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_nz_31_22[31:22];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_pd_enum {
            power_down = 0x0 { name = "Powered down"; desc = "powered down"; };
            normal = 0x1 { name = "Normal operation"; desc = "normal operation"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "APLL power-down control";
            desc = "APLL power-down control. The name is historic: 1 = running, 0 = powered down";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_pd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_pd[21:21];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_foutvcopd_enum {
            off = 0x0 { name = "No clock output"; desc = "no clock output"; };
            on = 0x1 { name = "Normal clock output"; desc = "normal clock output"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "APLL VCO output power-down control";
            desc = "APLL VCO output power-down control (1 = VCO output enabled)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_foutvcopd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_foutvcopd[20:20];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_postdivpd_enum {
            off = 0x0 { name = "No clock output"; desc = "no clock output"; };
            on = 0x1 { name = "Normal clock output"; desc = "normal clock output"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "APLL POSTDIV output power-down control";
            desc = "APLL POSTDIV output power-down control (1 = output enabled)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_postdivpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_postdivpd[19:19];

        enum PERI_CRG1_apll_fout4phasepd_enum {
            off = 0x0 { name = "No clock output"; desc = "no clock output"; };
            on = 0x1 { name = "Normal clock output"; desc = "normal clock output"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "APLL FOUT1PH0/FOUT2/FOUT3/FOUT4 output power-down control";
            desc = "APLL FOUT1PH0/FOUT2/FOUT3/FOUT4 output power-down control (1 = outputs enabled)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG1_apll_fout4phasepd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_fout4phasepd[18:18];

        field {
            name = "Reference clock divider";
            desc = "Reference clock divider (REFDIV) of the APLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x3;
        } apll_refdiv[17:12];

        field {
            name = "Integer multiplication factor";
            desc = "Integer multiplication factor (FBDIV) of the APLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x64;
        } apll_fbdiv[11:0];
    } PERI_CRG1 @ 0x0004;

    reg {
        name = "VPLL0 configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG2 is the VPLL0 configuration register 0.

VPLL0 (PERI_CRG2/3) generates the VOSD module clock. Reset: postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 2, refdiv = 1, fbdiv = 45 -> VCO 24 x 45 = 1080 MHz, POSTDIV output 540 MHz.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG2 (offset 0x8, printed page 3-18, `hi3516v100--Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 10301).";

        field {
            name = "Reserved in the bit table";
            desc = "Reserved in the bit table, but the data sheet total reset value of this register has these bits set (reset 0x1).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_nz_31_31[31:31];

        enum PERI_CRG2_vpll0_bypass_enum {
            no_bypass = 0x0 { name = "Not bypassed"; desc = "not bypassed"; };
            bypass = 0x1 { name = "Bypassed"; desc = "bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "VPLL0 clock divider bypass control";
            desc = "VPLL0 clock divider bypass control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG2_vpll0_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll0_bypass[30:30];

        field {
            name = "Second-stage output divider";
            desc = "Second-stage output divider (POSTDIV2) of the VPLL0";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } vpll0_postdiv2[29:27];

        field {
            name = "First-stage output divider";
            desc = "First-stage output divider (POSTDIV1) of the VPLL0";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2;
        } vpll0_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "Fractional part of the VPLL0 multiplication factor";
            desc = "Fractional part of the VPLL0 multiplication factor (frac / 2^24)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll0_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG2 @ 0x0008;

    reg {
        name = "VPLL0 configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG3 is the VPLL0 configuration register 1.

Reset 0x006C102D: refdiv 1, fbdiv 45 (VCO 1080 MHz), the VCO output enable (bit 20) is 0 at reset. Bit 22 reads 1 at reset although the bit table calls it reserved. [inferred] The Hi3520D/Hi3518 PLL registers have dsmpd at this bit (1 = integer mode, reset 1) and dacpd at bit 23; this data sheet documents neither, so treat bit 22 as probably dsmpd and leave it at 1. Lock status: PERI_CRG43 bit 1. To stop VPLL0 write bit 21 = 0.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG3 (offset 0xC, printed page 3-18, `hi3516v100--Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 10338).";

        field {
            name = "Reserved in the bit table";
            desc = "Reserved in the bit table, but the data sheet total reset value of this register has these bits set (reset 0x1).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_nz_31_22[31:22];

        enum PERI_CRG3_vpll0_pd_enum {
            power_down = 0x0 { name = "Powered down"; desc = "powered down"; };
            normal = 0x1 { name = "Normal operation"; desc = "normal operation"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "VPLL0 power-down control";
            desc = "VPLL0 power-down control. The name is historic: 1 = running, 0 = powered down";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_vpll0_pd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } vpll0_pd[21:21];

        enum PERI_CRG3_vpll0_foutvcopd_enum {
            off = 0x0 { name = "No clock output"; desc = "no clock output"; };
            on = 0x1 { name = "Normal clock output"; desc = "normal clock output"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "VPLL0 VCO output power-down control";
            desc = "VPLL0 VCO output power-down control (1 = VCO output enabled)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_vpll0_foutvcopd_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll0_foutvcopd[20:20];

        enum PERI_CRG3_vpll0_postdivpd_enum {
            off = 0x0 { name = "No clock output"; desc = "no clock output"; };
            on = 0x1 { name = "Normal clock output"; desc = "normal clock output"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "VPLL0 POSTDIV output power-down control";
            desc = "VPLL0 POSTDIV output power-down control (1 = output enabled)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_vpll0_postdivpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } vpll0_postdivpd[19:19];

        enum PERI_CRG3_vpll0_fout4phasepd_enum {
            off = 0x0 { name = "No clock output"; desc = "no clock output"; };
            on = 0x1 { name = "Normal clock output"; desc = "normal clock output"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "VPLL0 FOUT1PH0/FOUT2/FOUT3/FOUT4 output power-down control";
            desc = "VPLL0 FOUT1PH0/FOUT2/FOUT3/FOUT4 output power-down control (1 = outputs enabled)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG3_vpll0_fout4phasepd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } vpll0_fout4phasepd[18:18];

        field {
            name = "Reference clock divider";
            desc = "Reference clock divider (REFDIV) of the VPLL0";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } vpll0_refdiv[17:12];

        field {
            name = "Integer multiplication factor";
            desc = "Integer multiplication factor (FBDIV) of the VPLL0";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2D;
        } vpll0_fbdiv[11:0];
    } PERI_CRG3 @ 0x000C;

    reg {
        name = "VPLL1 configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG4 is the VPLL1 configuration register 0.

VPLL1 (PERI_CRG4/5) generates the VOHD module clock. Reset: postdiv2 = 2, postdiv1 = 4, refdiv = 2, fbdiv = 99 -> VCO 24 x 99 / 2 = 1188 MHz, POSTDIV output 148.5 MHz. The data sheet example (3.2.3) feeds the VOU 74.25 MHz clock from FOUTPOSTDIV / 2 with exactly these settings; its arithmetic line prints `= 1485 MHz` for the 1188 MHz VCO, a typo (24 x 99 / 2 = 1188).

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG4 (offset 0x10, printed page 3-19, `hi3516v100--Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 10393).";

        field {
            name = "Reserved in the bit table";
            desc = "Reserved in the bit table, but the data sheet total reset value of this register has these bits set (reset 0x1).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_nz_31_31[31:31];

        enum PERI_CRG4_vpll1_bypass_enum {
            no_bypass = 0x0 { name = "Not bypassed"; desc = "not bypassed"; };
            bypass = 0x1 { name = "Bypassed"; desc = "bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "VPLL1 clock divider bypass control";
            desc = "VPLL1 clock divider bypass control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG4_vpll1_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll1_bypass[30:30];

        field {
            name = "Second-stage output divider";
            desc = "Second-stage output divider (POSTDIV2) of the VPLL1";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2;
        } vpll1_postdiv2[29:27];

        field {
            name = "First-stage output divider";
            desc = "First-stage output divider (POSTDIV1) of the VPLL1";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x4;
        } vpll1_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "Fractional part of the VPLL1 multiplication factor";
            desc = "Fractional part of the VPLL1 multiplication factor (frac / 2^24)";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } vpll1_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG4 @ 0x0010;

    reg {
        name = "VPLL1 configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG5 is the VPLL1 configuration register 1.

Reset 0x007C2063: refdiv 2, fbdiv 99. Bit 22 reads 1 at reset although the bit table calls it reserved. [inferred] The Hi3520D/Hi3518 PLL registers have dsmpd at this bit (1 = integer mode, reset 1) and dacpd at bit 23; this data sheet documents neither, so treat bit 22 as probably dsmpd and leave it at 1. Lock status: PERI_CRG43 bit 2. To stop VPLL1 write bit 21 = 0.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG5 (offset 0x14, printed page 3-20, `hi3516v100--Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 10439).";

        field {
            name = "Reserved in the bit table";
            desc = "Reserved in the bit table, but the data sheet total reset value of this register has these bits set (reset 0x1).";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x1;
        } reserved_nz_31_22[31:22];

        enum PERI_CRG5_vpll1_pd_enum {
            power_down = 0x0 { name = "Powered down"; desc = "powered down"; };
            normal = 0x1 { name = "Normal operation"; desc = "normal operation"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "VPLL1 power-down control";
            desc = "VPLL1 power-down control. The name is historic: 1 = running, 0 = powered down";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG5_vpll1_pd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } vpll1_pd[21:21];

        enum PERI_CRG5_vpll1_foutvcopd_enum {
