A9 frequency (data sheet 3.2.3, Table 3-4): a9_max_freq_mode selects the maximum frequency mode (0: A9 max 800 MHz with APLL FOUTPOSTDIV = 800 MHz; 1: A9 max 750 MHz with APLL FOUTPOSTDIV = 1500 MHz). It cannot be switched dynamically and may only be written before the SLOW -> NORMAL switch. a9_axi_freq_mode sets the A9:AXI ratio and can be switched dynamically; 4:1 is not supported when a9_max_freq_mode = 1. The A9 runs from XIN (24 MHz) after reset (SLOW mode). The vendor U-Boot header arch-hi3520d/platform.h (REG_CRG8_OFFSET, BITOFFSET_A9_MAX_FREQUENCY, BITOFFSET_A9_AXI_FRE_SCALE; unused Hi3516-template leftover) uses this very layout (bit 0, bits 2:1). Reset value 0x10: cpu__srst_req (bit 4) is the only set bit. Low confidence: the data sheet names this bit `cpu__srst_req` (double underscore), resets it to 1 and says it is only valid in slave-load mode; the Hi3520D data sheet has the equivalent field one bit higher and a read-only reserved bit 4 that reads 1 on real hardware, so this bit probably does not hold the running CPU in reset. Preserve bit 4 on writes.

