    reg {
        name = "VIU (ISP) clock and reset configuration register";
        desc = "PERI_CRG16 is the VIU (ISP) clock and reset configuration register.

VI interface clocks (data sheet 3.2.3, Table 3-7). The doubling DLL is needed only for double-edge capture: release vi_dll_rst (only after the system is in NORMAL mode) and then set vi0/vi1_dll_bypass = 1 (DLL enabled); for single-edge capture leave the DLL in reset and bypassed. Low confidence: the data sheet describes vi_dll_rst as 0 = reset, 1 = release and says it is held in reset by default, but its reset value is 1; the polarity is the opposite of the other *_rst_req bits. The register field description is followed here. The vi*_dll_bypass bits are named `bypass` but 1 enables the DLL (data sheet). Reset 0xCF: bits 7:6 read 1 although the bit table calls them reserved.

Data sheet 3.2.5 PERI_CRG16 (offset 0x40, printed page 3-32, `hi3516v100--Hi3516-Datasheet.txt` line 11064).";

